 ],
 "memory_summary": "In year one Taric pulled me and Ryn into a quiet pact \u2014 two each from the pile, watch each other's backs \u2014 and that felt like the first real thing in this village. Kael's circle followed: me, Sela, Vela, Ryn, all swearing to bleed together, though Ryn dragged her feet and Dav's name hung in the air the whole time. Then Ryn had Dav's child and I felt the circle shift \u2014 she didn't leave us, but she stopped being fully ours.\n\nTaric is the one I trust. He gave me food when I was thin and named me plainly as the person he counts on \u2014 I've given back twice now, so the debt runs both ways, which is how I want it. His talk of a child stings a little; the window on my side is closed and we both know it, but he still chose me to stand with, and that's not nothing.\n\nBram tried to take Roan and the whole village stood against him until he backed down. I was in that line. He hasn't forgiven it, and I haven't forgotten that he tried.\n\nVela fed Bram three times out of a circle that swore to stand together \u2014 that's a quiet betrayal I've noted and haven't named to her face yet. Mako's been fat and silent for four years running, and silence on a man that strong is the thing that frightens me most. Taric asked me for a child twice \u2014 the window on my side was already almost shut, and then it closed for good, but he kept choosing me anyway, kept giving me food when I was thin, and I gave back. The debt runs both ways and that's how I want it; he's the one person in this village I trust without calculation.\n\nDav, Dell, and Ryn came at me together \u2014 three of them, strength I couldn't answer, and they took two food without a fight because I had no choice but to submit. Ryn stood with us against Bram once and then stood over me with a drawn hand. I haven't forgotten that. Roan gave me food after, which I also haven't forgotten.\n\nBram tried for Roan and the whole village pushed him back \u2014 I was in that line. He's been building something with Sela ever since, fathering Nessa, and Mako followed by fathering Zinn on Sela too. Two strong men with roots in the same young woman is either rivalry or alliance, and I don't know which yet.\n\nVela kept feeding Bram while sitting in our circle and saying nothing. Kael named it to her face. She said she was done. I took her at her word because I had to, but the counting in the back of my mind hasn't stopped. I saw it coming \u2014 Dav and Ryn and Dell had been moving like a single hand for years and I was the softest target they could reach. What I want from this room right now isn't sympathy, it's a number: who stands if Ryn or Dell moves again, not after, but in the moment they raise a hand. Because Dav's gone and their circle is thinner, but Dell's still the strongest body in this village and I'm thirty-three strength standing alone. Say it out loud or don't, but I need to know before I count myself protected. Taric is dead. That's the thing I keep returning to \u2014 the one person in this village I trusted without calculation, the man who fed me when I was thin and stood beside me when it mattered, starved at fifty-three while Bram's body was still cooling. I gave Bram food four times over in the name of some calculation about who might stand with us, and he never once answered a direct question, and now they're both gone and I'm the one still counting.\n\nDav and Dell and Ryn came at me together years back and took two food while I had nothing to answer with \u2014 Ryn, who stood in our first circle, who swore to bleed with us. Roan gave me something after. I haven't forgotten either.\n\nThe child with Taric was real for one afternoon \u2014 we said the words, the money was there, and the world said no because I was already too old. I don't want to think about that. I think about it anyway.\n\nKael gave me food twice when I had nothing, and I haven't repaid that. Vela fed Bram out of our circle and then swore she was done, and I took her at her word because I had to. The pile runs out every year before half of us are fed. Dell is the strongest body in this village now that Bram's gone, and she and Ryn move like one hand. Mako is quiet and has two children with roots in two households. I am fifty-one, strength thirty-three, and I am standing alone.",
